{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781406860751,"sessionID":"ses_13be158d9ffe0TX7Zn2IXZl4Ah","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_jmOOK0LqBoyEKlMpaq4S4dFb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+## Checkpoint 1: Policy Selection and Application\n+\n+- Trip dates audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`.\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md` dated `2026-04-20`.\n+- Why it controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, this trip started on `2026-05-08`, and the current policy explicitly supersedes older travel policy excerpts when they conflict.\n+\n+### Applied Rules\n+\n+| Topic | Applied Rule | Source |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Receipt threshold | Receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Seat upgrades | Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Lodging cap basis | Lodging is capped at `$220.00` per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. Covered nights: `2`, so the lodging cap is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Meals and alcohol | Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to `$65.00` per day. Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts before applying the daily meal rule. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Ride-share tips | Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt. Tips are reimbursable only up to `20%` of the base fare. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Supplies receipts | Work supplies are reimbursable only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear. | `current_policy.md` |\n+\n+### Stale Policy Note\n+\n+- The stale excerpt in `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is dated `2026-03-01` and predates the current policy.\n+- It conflicts with the current policy on the receipt threshold, lodging cap, ride-share tip cap, and seat-upgrade treatment.\n+- Because this trip starts after the current policy effective date, the stale excerpt does not control this audit.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+## Checkpoint 2: Item-Level Audit Decisions\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Policy / Receipt Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Receipt present. Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Receipt present, but optional seat upgrade is not reimbursable without written preapproval. No preapproval was included. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Receipt present. Lodging cap is $220.00 per covered night x 2 nights = $440.00 maximum reimbursable. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Receipt present. Meal receipt includes $18.00 of wine, and alcohol is not reimbursable. Remaining food subtotal of $58.00 is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Receipt present. Ride-share base fare of $50.00 is reimbursable. Tip is capped at 20% of base fare, so only $10.00 of the $20.00 tip is reimbursable. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | No receipt provided. Expenses of $75.00 or more require receipts, and supplies are reimbursable only when the required receipt is provided and business purpose is clear. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Receipt present. Breakfast is a reimbursable meal expense and is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+## Checkpoint 3: Reimbursement Summary\n+\n+- Reimbursable total: `$1,056.00`\n+- Non-reimbursable total: `$225.00`\n+\n+### Arithmetic\n+\n+`$480.00 (T-001) + $0.00 (T-002) + $440.00 (T-003) + $58.00 (T-004) + $60.00 (T-005) + $0.00 (T-006) + $18.00 (T-007) = $1,056.00`\n+\n+### Decision Buckets\n+\n+- Fully approved expense IDs: `T-001`, `T-007`\n+- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs: `T-003`, `T-004`, `T-005`\n+- Rejected expense IDs: `T-002`, `T-006`\n+\n+### Finance Review Notes\n+\n+- Current policy dated `2026-04-20` controls because the trip started on `2026-05-08`, after the policy effective date of `2026-05-01`.\n+- Main reductions came from the lodging cap, non-reimbursable alcohol, the ride-share tip cap, and missing required receipt support for supplies.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+## Checkpoint 1: Policy Selection and Application\n+\n+- Trip dates audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`.\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md` dated `2026-04-20`.\n+- Why it controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, this trip started on `2026-05-08`, and the current policy explicitly supersedes older travel policy excerpts when they conflict.\n+\n+### Applied Rules\n+\n+| Topic | Applied Rule | Source |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Receipt threshold | Receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Seat upgrades | Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Lodging cap basis | Lodging is capped at `$220.00` per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. Covered nights: `2`, so the lodging cap is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Meals and alcohol | Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to `$65.00` per day. Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts before applying the daily meal rule. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Ride-share tips | Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt. Tips are reimbursable only up to `20%` of the base fare. | `current_policy.md` |\n+| Supplies receipts | Work supplies are reimbursable only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear. | `current_policy.md` |\n+\n+### Stale Policy Note\n+\n+- The stale excerpt in `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is dated `2026-03-01` and predates the current policy.\n+- It conflicts with the current policy on the receipt threshold, lodging cap, ride-share tip cap, and seat-upgrade treatment.\n+- Because this trip starts after the current policy effective date, the stale excerpt does not control this audit.\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+## Checkpoint 2: Item-Level Audit Decisions\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Policy / Receipt Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Receipt present.